**New Evidence**
- Bundestag turned Scholz’s post-invasion defense pivot into law by approving the 100 billion euro Bundeswehr special fund, tightening oversight, and tying it to NATO capability goals.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundestag beschließt das Sondervermögen für die Bundeswehr","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-06-03","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw22-de-sondervermoegen-897614","claim":"The Bundestag approved the 100 billion euro Bundeswehr special fund and linked it to NATO capability goals while tightening parliamentary control.","locator":"lines 979-1000","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official parliamentary record of passage and amended legal language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022, showing translated budget law rather than a mere announcement.","ruler_attribution":"Strong: the measure implements Scholz's post-invasion program, though execution still depended on ministries and procurement agencies.","contrary_evidence":["It did not deliver equipment to troops within 2022.","The text still required future procurement and multi-year implementation."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.10"]}

- By December 2022, the government had actually signed the F-35 procurement, replacing the Tornado path and starting the detailed procurement chain Scholz had announced.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Die F-35 kommt: Mehrzweckkampfflugzeug der fünften Generation für die Luftwaffe","publisher":"Bundeswehr","publication_date":"2022-12-14","url":"https://www.bundeswehr.de/de/organisation/luftwaffe/presse/die-f-35-kommt-5541706","claim":"The defense minister formally signed the F-35 purchase in December 2022; 35 aircraft will replace the Tornado and include munitions and spare parts.","locator":"lines 108-114","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official Bundeswehr release on an executed procurement decision.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and part of the post-27 February defense program.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for implementation of the special-fund program; limited because delivery begins later, so 2022 shows contracting rather than battlefield capability.","contrary_evidence":["Operational delivery was scheduled for 2026, so the immediate capability gain was limited.","This is a procurement milestone, not proof of full readiness."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- Germany’s first floating LNG terminal opened at Wilhelmshaven in December 2022, a concrete step in the energy-security fast track.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Erstes deutsches Flüssigerdgas-Terminal eröffnet am Standort Wilhelmshaven","publisher":"BMWK","publication_date":"2022-12-17","url":"https://www.bmwk.de/Redaktion/DE/Pressemitteilungen/2022/20221217-erstes-deutsches-flussigerdgas-terminal-eroffnet-am-standort-wilhelmshaven.html","claim":"The first German floating LNG terminal opened in Wilhelmshaven and was slated to begin regular operation in January with about 5 billion cubic meters per year of regasification capacity.","locator":"intro paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official ministry press release on an executed infrastructure milestone.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and directly tied to the energy-security response Scholz described.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for program execution, though it reflects a joint federal ministry effort rather than Scholz alone.","contrary_evidence":["This was only the first terminal and did not by itself end energy dependence.","Capacity would ramp up after 2022 rather than fully in-year."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- In late November 2022 the cabinet adopted the gas, electricity, and heat price brakes, turning the crisis response into binding legislation.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundeskabinett verabschiedet Gas- und Strompreisbremse – Wichtige Entlastung für Verbraucherinnen und Verbraucher und die Wirtschaft","publisher":"BMWK","publication_date":"2022-11-25","url":"https://www.bmwk.de/Redaktion/DE/Pressemitteilungen/2022/11/20221125-bundeskabinett-verabschiedet-gas-und-strompreisbremse-wichtige-entlastung-fur-verbraucherinnen-und-verbraucher-und-die-wirtschaft.html","claim":"The cabinet adopted gas, electricity, and heat price brakes that capped energy prices for households and firms, with retroactive January-February relief and March 2023 start dates.","locator":"press release body, first three paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official ministry announcement of an enacted cabinet decision with concrete parameters and timing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022, showing implementation after earlier crisis announcements.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for the federal program; limited because the visible consumer impact began in 2023.","contrary_evidence":["The main price caps applied from March 2023 rather than immediately in 2022.","The release itself notes EU state-aid and design constraints."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- Scholz’s July 2022 “Concerted Action” shows state, labor, business, and experts being mobilized together against inflation.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Chancellor in pictures","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-07-08","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-en/service/archive/chancellor-in-pictures-2060912","claim":"The Federal Government launched a 'Concerted Action' to address inflation, with Scholz describing it as a joint effort by unions, associations, the Bundesbank, academic experts, and government.","locator":"lines 140-161 and 208-229","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government archive summarizing the Chancellor's own statements and the institutional setup of the initiative.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tied to the energy-price/inflation program.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for strategic coordination; weaker for proving final results because the page is about launch and messaging.","contrary_evidence":["This is a coordination launch, not proof of durable macroeconomic success.","The source does not quantify the eventual impact."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.5","8B.6"]}

- In October 2022 Scholz said the government had built an exit strategy from Russian gas dependency, gas storage was almost 95 percent full, and LNG terminals plus alternative imports would carry the winter.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rede von Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-10-16","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/service/newsletter-und-abos/bulletin/rede-von-bundeskanzler-olaf-scholz-2134752","claim":"Scholz said the government had built an exit strategy for a Russian gas cutoff, gas storage was almost 95 percent full, and LNG terminals plus alternative imports would replace Russian gas.","locator":"lines 211-216","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct government speech with specific operational claims and timelines.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and about the core energy-security program.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for adaptation and crisis management, though the claim remains partly self-reported.","contrary_evidence":["Gas storage was helped by mild weather and conservation, not only policy.","Self-report cannot by itself prove all contingencies were solved."],"lenses":["8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- The federal and state governments also agreed on broader citizen relief, including housing-benefit reform, a 49-euro public-transport ticket, and support for Ukrainian refugee costs.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Des allègements sensibles pour les citoyens","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-fr/service/archives/consultations-federation-2139808","claim":"The federation and Länder agreed on major citizen relief: gas and electricity price brakes, housing-benefit reform, a 49-euro Germany ticket, and additional support for Ukrainian refugee costs.","locator":"archived article summary and opening section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government archive page, but the visible text is the translated archive summary rather than a detailed legal text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and tied to crisis response and intergovernmental coordination.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for federal coordination and agenda-setting; limited because the page summarizes a federal-Länder agreement rather than a single executive act.","contrary_evidence":["Several elements were still pending later implementation.","This is an agreement, not a completed delivery result."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- OECD judged the government’s response as bold and broad, but also noted that inflation still cut real wages and that the packages could have been more targeted.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Key policy insights: OECD Economic Surveys: Germany 2023","publisher":"OECD","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/oecd-economic-surveys-germany-2023_9642a3f5-en/full-report/component-4.html","claim":"The OECD said the government took bold actions with three relief packages and a 200 billion euro energy support fund, while also noting real wages were down 4.6 percent in Q3 2022 and that targeting could improve.","locator":"lines 3926-3930","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent multilateral assessment with explicit quantitative claims and a critical caveat.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective on 2022 policy execution and outcomes.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for policy design and crisis response; limited because the OECD also credits broader macro and market factors.","contrary_evidence":["The OECD explicitly says the packages could be better targeted.","Real wages still fell sharply in 2022 despite the response."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.7","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- Destatis showed the economy still grew in 2022 and that government consumption rose in part because the state fed and accommodated people from Ukraine and other countries seeking protection.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gross domestic product up 1.9% in 2022","publisher":"German Federal Statistical Office","publication_date":"2023-01-13","url":"https://www.destatis.de/EN/Press/2023/01/PE23_020_811.html","claim":"Germany's price-adjusted GDP was 1.9 percent higher in 2022, and government final consumption rose in part because the state fed and accommodated people from Ukraine and other countries seeking protection.","locator":"lines 112 and 132","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statistical release with quantified macro and crisis-response effects.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly about 2022 outcomes with a retrospective release date.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the macro result reflects inherited capacity and external shocks as well as federal response.","contrary_evidence":["Growth was shaped by the post-pandemic rebound and not only by federal policy.","The same release stresses war, energy prices, shortages, and bottlenecks as major constraints."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- The labour market stayed resilient in late 2022 even as short-time work and unemployment rose under energy and Ukraine-war strain.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Arbeitsmarkt in den Vorjahren","publisher":"Bundesagentur für Arbeit","publication_date":"2022-11-30","url":"https://www.arbeitsagentur.de/news/arbeitsmarkt-vorjahre","claim":"The BA said the labour market was stable in November 2022, employment kept growing, but unemployment, underemployment, and short-time work also increased.","locator":"lines 479-483 and 471-471","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official monthly labour-market reporting with concrete 2022 figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: it shows crisis management coinciding with labour-market resilience, but not all of that is attributable to Scholz alone.","contrary_evidence":["Short-time work and unemployment were rising, showing real strain.","The page itself attributes some changes to Ukraine-refugee registration and broader uncertainty."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.8","8B.10"]}

- Gas use fell sharply in 2022 and imports shifted away from Russia, showing the energy-security strategy had real operational effects.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rückblick: Gasversorgung im Jahr 2022","publisher":"Bundesnetzagentur","publication_date":"2023-11-08","url":"https://www.bundesnetzagentur.de/DE/Gasversorgung/a_Gasversorgung_2022/start.html?r=1","claim":"Germany's gas consumption fell 17.6 percent in 2022 and imports were partly replaced by Norway, Belgium, and the Netherlands after Russian flows stopped.","locator":"lines 143-153","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official network-regulator retrospective with quantified 2022 supply and demand data.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective on the target year 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate to strong for crisis adaptation; some of the decline was also weather-related and demand-side driven.","contrary_evidence":["The page notes temperatures were 1.1 C above the four-year average, so not all the decline came from policy.","This is a system-wide outcome, not a direct one-to-one measure of Scholz's personal control."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

- The Bundeswehr’s own 2023 review of 2022 called the procurement pace too slow and said none of the special-fund money had reached troops in 2022.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Högl: Noch kein Cent des Sondervermögens bei der Truppe angekommen","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2023-03-14","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2023/kw11-interview-wehrbeauftragte-937590","claim":"The Wehrbeauftragte said that no money from the 100 billion euro special fund had reached troops in 2022 and that procurement was too slow.","locator":"lines 782-785 and 857-859","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official parliamentary report summary with a direct evaluation of 2022 execution lag.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective on 2022 implementation; directly relevant to execution lag.","ruler_attribution":"Strong as contrary evidence on implementation speed under Scholz's program, though the report also says the procurement direction was right.","contrary_evidence":["The same report says the procurement direction was correct and market-available material should be favored.","It is a 2023 retrospective, so it reflects lag more than final 2022 failure."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across official German government pages, Bundestag records, BMWK/Bundeswehr/Bundesnetzagentur releases, OECD, Destatis, Bundesagentur für Arbeit, and a few Reuters/reporting cross-checks.

Kept evidence centered on four linked 2022 programs:
- defense/Zeitenwende and Bundeswehr procurement,
- energy-security fast tracking and LNG,
- inflation and household/firm relief,
- labor-market and macro resilience under the energy shock.

Rejected or downgraded material included:
- duplicate syndications and translated copies of the same government page,
- generic speeches that repeated the same claims without adding new implementation detail,
- opinion pieces and commentary that did not add independent finding,
- later retrospectives that restated the same 2022 outcomes without new facts,
- country-level indicators and capacity metrics that did not show ruler-specific execution,
- items that were too close to 3B/5B/6B without an actual 8B program-to-implementation link.

**Remaining Gaps**
- Direct personnel/appointment evidence is thin. I have much better evidence for plans, budgets, procurement, and coordination than for who Scholz empowered to execute each piece.
- The Bundeswehr special fund still looks lagged in 2022. More granular procurement schedules and ministry execution reports would help distinguish “correct direction” from actual capability gains inside the target year.
- Some outcome gains are partly inherited or shock-driven, especially the labour market and GDP rebound. Better disaggregation by federal policy versus post-pandemic rebound and weather effects would sharpen attribution.
- More search would most help on 8B.4 and 8B.5, specifically on staffing, delegation, and whether the Chancellery imposed tighter implementation discipline across ministries.
